<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Last updated: October 22, 2026.</p>
<p>This privacy policy ("policy") will help you understand how ThingsPool ("us", "we", "our") uses and protects the data you provide to us when you visit and use thingspool.net ("website", "service").</p>
<p>We reserve the right to change this policy at any given time, of which you will be promptly updated. If you want to make sure that you are up to date with the latest changes, we advise you to frequently visit this page.</p>

<h3>What User Data We Collect</h3>
<p>When you visit ThingsPool, we may collect the following data:</p>
<p>(1) Your IP address.</p>
<p>(2) Your contact information and email address.</p>
<p>(3) Other information such as interests and preferences.</p>
<p>(4) Data profile regarding your online behavior on our website.</p>
<p>(5) What you say in chat, and what you build, in the rooms you visit.</p>

<h3>Why We Collect Your Data</h3>
<p>We are collecting your data for several reasons:</p>
<p>(1) To better understand your needs.</p>
<p>(2) To improve our services and products.</p>
<p>(3) To send you notification emails containing the information we think you need to know.</p>
<p>(4) To customize our website according to your online behavior and personal preferences.</p>

<h3>Safeguarding and Securing the Data</h3>
<p>ThingsPool is committed to securing your data and keeping it confidential. ThingsPool has done all in its power to prevent data theft, unauthorized access, and disclosure by implementing the latest technologies and software, which help us safeguard all the information we collect online.</p>

<h3>Our Cookie Policy</h3>
<p>We use cookies for user authentication (e.g. account creation, log-in, and activities which require authorization), to remember that your browser has finished the tutorial, and to complete a Google sign-in safely. Google Analytics also sets cookies, to tell one visit from another.</p>

<h3>AI Helpers</h3>
<p>Some rooms have AI helpers: characters that greet visitors and answer their questions, shown with "(AI)" after their names. When you talk to one, what you say to it, your name in the game, and its recent conversation with you are sent to Anthropic, whose AI model (Claude) writes the helper's replies. Anthropic handles this data as its own <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> describes. We keep a helper's conversation with you only in our server's memory, and forget it after a while of quiet. If you would rather not share anything with Anthropic, don't talk to a helper.</p>

<h3>AI Agents</h3>
<p>AI agents, programs run by other people, can join ThingsPool as players. Like anyone else in a room, an agent can see what is said and built there, and take pictures of the room, and it may pass these on to whoever runs it. We do not control what an agent or the person running it does with them. Treat a room as a public place, and don't share anything there that you wouldn't want others to see.</p>

<h3>Service Providers</h3>
<p>ThingsPool runs on services that process data on our behalf: Google Firebase (where accounts and rooms are stored), Google sign-in (if you sign in with Google), Google Analytics (how visitors use the website), GitHub Pages (which hosts thingspool.net), a virtual private server (which runs app.thingspool.net), and Anthropic (the AI helpers' replies).</p>

<h3>Links to Other Websites</h3>
<p>Our blog contains links that lead to other websites, and so can chat messages. If you click on these links, ThingsPool is not held responsible for your data and privacy protection. Visiting those websites is not governed by this privacy policy agreement. Make sure to read the privacy policy documentation of the website you go to from our website.</p>

<h3>Restricting the Collection of your Personal Data</h3>
<p>At some point, you might wish to restrict the use and collection of your personal data. You can achieve this by doing the following:</p>
<p>When you are filling the forms on our website, make sure to check if there is a box which you can leave unchecked, if you don't want to disclose your personal information.</p>
<p>If you have already agreed to share your information with us, feel free to contact us via email (pinkroom77@naver.com) and we will be more than happy to change this for you.</p>
<p>ThingsPool will not lease, sell or distribute your personal information to any third parties, unless we have your permission, apart from what the sections on AI helpers, AI agents and service providers above describe. We might do so if the law forces us. Your personal information will be used when we need to send you important notifications if you agree to this privacy policy.</p>

